Formatted Tables: knitr::kable()
```{r}
#| label: tbl-top-counties
#| tbl-cap: "Top 10 county-season combinations by total deer harvest."

deer |&gt;
  group_by(county, season) |&gt;
  summarize(total = sum(harvest_count, na.rm = TRUE), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  slice_max(total, n = 10) |&gt;
  rename(County = county, Season = season, `Total Harvest` = total) |&gt;
  knitr::kable()
```
In prose: "County leaders are listed in @tbl-top-counties."

Speaker Notes: kable() is the simplest path to a formatted HTML table. It respects column names, so rename() before kable() is good practice. The label must start with tbl- for table cross-references. Show the rendered output side by side with the raw tibble print — the difference is obvious. If students want more control over column formatting, cell colors, or footnotes, point them toward gt() as an extension.

