Step 4: Summarize EPT Richness
ept_summary &lt;- filtered |&gt;
  filter(order_name %in% c("ephemeroptera", "plecoptera", "trichoptera")) |&gt;
  group_by(SiteID) |&gt;
  summarize(
    ept_richness  = n_distinct(order_name),
    ept_abundance = sum(count),
    stream_order  = first(stream_order),
    .groups = "drop"
  )
Checkpoint: Which site has the highest EPT richness?

Speaker Notes: The key conceptual question here is: why n_distinct(order_name) and not n()? n() counts rows. n_distinct(order_name) counts how many of the three EPT orders are actually represented. A site with 100 mayflies but no stoneflies or caddisflies has EPT richness of 1, not 100. This distinction between richness (diversity) and abundance (quantity) is fundamental in ecology and worth spending 3-4 minutes on.

